the deadly shooting raises new questions  about school and government officials  efforts to keep students safe 33 states  including Florida require every school  or school district to have a  comprehensive safety or emergency plan  Adriana Diaz is at Stoneman Douglas High  School in parkland that you're on a good  morning good morning in a cruel twist  the school was reportedly planning an  active shooter drill in just a few weeks  but it's unclear if any planning or  preparation could have stopped the  gunman all entrances at Marjory Stoneman  Douglas High School are locked during  the school day reopening when students  leave that's when police say the  suspected gunman set off a fire alarm  and then opened fire  in school drills like this our common  nationwide to prepare for active shooter  situation teachers at Stoneman Douglas  were trained on what to do with such an  event but while some students report  going through an active shooter drill at  the school others received less training  we did have meetings with our teachers  about where we need to go what we should  do in these situations but we never had  an active shooter drill a lockdown was  effective in keeping a shooter out of a  California school last year because  officials had advanced notice he was  approaching  but the same plan in Florida Wednesday  turned chaotic because there was no such  notice and the accused shooter set off a  fire alarm sending students rushing out  of their classrooms when the gunman was  already on campus former police officer  Adam Caron teaches students how to deal  with active shooter scenarios the  situation is very fluid so to say that  you have a one-size-fits-all model for a  dynamic situation may not be the total  solution  he says training is important but it may  be impossible to keep students 100% safe  if somebody really wanted to get into  the school with this malicious intent  they could have no matter what and I  don't think any security feature really  could have prevented that other than a  prison the school locks its doors during  the school day but they do not have  metal detectors and the expert we spoke  to said that a lockdown could be the  safest scenario in some school shootings  but not all Gayle Adrianna thank you  very much
 

